# LAMMPS (stable_30Sep2026, GRANULAR) equivalent of in.bedd: same data, dt, skin,
# Hertz normal with material E, nu; Mindlin tangential (stiffness from material,
# no-slip -> Coulomb mu), Tsuji damping from e (LIGGGHTS uses its own beta mapping),
# primitive floor. Differences: damping law details, LAMMPS sort bin = 0.5 cutoff (default).
variable px index *
variable py index *
variable pz index *
processors ${px} ${py} ${pz}
units si
atom_style sphere
atom_modify map array
boundary p p f
newton off
comm_modify vel yes
read_data ${data}
neighbor 0.0005 bin
neigh_modify delay 0
timestep 1e-5
pair_style granular
pair_coeff * * hertz/material 5e6 0.3 0.45 tangential mindlin NULL 1.0 0.5 damping tsuji
fix zwall all wall/gran granular hertz/material 5e6 0.3 0.45 tangential mindlin NULL 1.0 0.5 damping tsuji zplane 0.0 NULL
fix gravi all gravity 9.81 vector 0.0 0.0 -1.0
fix integr all nve/sphere
thermo_style custom step atoms ke
thermo 1000
run ${nsteps}
